\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Action space. All nine dimensions are emitted at every policy step by a policy conditioned on the image state and step index, so it can emit image- and step-dependent controls. In an evaluation replay the n$\to $p policy holds $a_0$, $a_4$, $a_5$, $a_7$ at or near their bounds and $a_6$ near-constant, varying $a_1$--$a_3$, $a_8$; the p$\to $n policy varies all nine (\S  \ref  {sec:limitations}). Because $a_7$ sits within 1\% of its upper bound on 97.5\% of n$\to $p steps, that bound may be binding; we did not train with a wider range. The $a_0$ range is the base strength $s$; pass $k$ of a step applies $\qopname  \relax m{min}(0.9,\ s\beta (1 + 0.15k))$, with $\beta $ from $a_6$, so applied strengths span $(0.17, 0.9]$. $^{\dagger }$Narrowed from $[0.5, 3.0]$ in an earlier code version (Supp.\nobreakspace  {}Table\nobreakspace  {}R5).\relax }}{3}{table.caption.9}}
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:action-space}{{1}{3}{Action space. All nine dimensions are emitted at every policy step by a policy conditioned on the image state and step index, so it can emit image- and step-dependent controls. In an evaluation replay the n$\to $p policy holds $a_0$, $a_4$, $a_5$, $a_7$ at or near their bounds and $a_6$ near-constant, varying $a_1$--$a_3$, $a_8$; the p$\to $n policy varies all nine (\S \ref {sec:limitations}). Because $a_7$ sits within 1\% of its upper bound on 97.5\% of n$\to $p steps, that bound may be binding; we did not train with a wider range. The $a_0$ range is the base strength $s$; pass $k$ of a step applies $\min (0.9,\ s\beta (1 + 0.15k))$, with $\beta $ from $a_6$, so applied strengths span $(0.17, 0.9]$. $^{\dagger }$Narrowed from $[0.5, 3.0]$ in an earlier code version (Supp.~Table~R5).\relax }{table.caption.9}{}}
